    "reconstruct_help": {
      "exit_code": 0,
      "stdout": "usage: reconstruct.py [-h] [-v VERSION] [--voxel-size VOXEL_SIZE]\n                      [--down-voxel DOWN_VOXEL] [--seed SEED] [--no-vis]\n                      --experiment EXPERIMENT [--selection-query QUERY.rq]\n                      [--override-experiment] [--no-write]\n\nReconstruct a capture (fullbatch or SPARQL-selected frames), print Mean L2,\nshow the cloud + trajectories.\n\noptional arguments:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -v VERSION, --version VERSION\n                        open3d or my_icp (default: the experiment's icpBackend\n                        setting, else open3d). Passing this AND an experiment\n                        that records a different backend is an error.\n  --voxel-size VOXEL_SIZE\n                        registration voxel size in metres (default: 0.05)\n  --down-voxel DOWN_VOXEL\n                        optional map-only voxel size in metres (default: no\n                        map downsampling)\n  --seed SEED           Open3D RANSAC seed (default: 0)\n  --no-vis              skip the Open3D window (print metrics only)\n  --experiment EXPERIMENT\n                        experiment Turtle (or its workspace directory); an\n                        UNSEALED declaration triggers the measuring first\n                        pass, which consumes the declared hw1:batchFile. The\n                        run value is written back below the machine marker.\n  --selection-query QUERY.rq\n                        SPARQL SELECT over --experiment binding ?frame (frame\n                        IRI) or ?frameIndex (integer). The bindings become the\n                        frame list; results are cut into contiguous segments.\n  --override-experiment, --write\n                        write run results to the experiment file (default: no-\n                        write / dry run)\n  --no-write            explicit dry run (default behavior): print the results\n                        but write nothing into the experiment file\n",
      "stderr": ""
    },
